+# Deploy-gating prevention layer — R55 option B landed, A routed (report-only brief)
+
+**Lane:** R55 (#2249, ecosystem-scout, Job 478520 03:25Z cycle, verdict `adapt`) — adopted in part this cycle. **Scope of this document:** consolidate the unrouted prevention surface the scout identified, land the one agent-executable option (B), and leave an honest maintainer-lane handoff for the rest. Nothing here duplicates the deploy-lane RCA (`docs/bridge/bridge-20261028-deploy-lane-rca.md`) — it extends it with the official capability surface and live probe receipts.
+
+## What landed (option B, in-repo, this PR)
+
+`infrastructure/mcp-control-plane/render.yaml` now declares `healthCheckPath: /health` for `supremeai-mcp-tower`. Receipts:
+
+- **Live probe (zero-credential, 2026-10-29 ~19:45Z):** `GET https://supremeai-mcp-tower.onrender.com/health` → **200/82ms**, body `{"status":"degraded","server":"supremeai-control-tower","version":"1.0.0","services":{"healthy":31,"degraded":2,...}}`. The endpoint exists on the deployed build today; the field merely wires Render's rollout gate to it.
+- **Transport-level, by design:** Render health checks pass on 2xx and ignore the body, so the gate discriminates *does the new container boot and serve* — exactly the signal the RCA said was missing ("the NEW container fails to serve, and Render marks the deploy `update_failed` after boot retries" with "no health-check signal"). The tower's own `status: degraded` subsystem view (31/33) does NOT fail the gate; subsystem health is the tower's internal concern, boot liveness is the deploy plane's.
+- **The class it closes:** P1 #2211's boot crash (`Tool system_parity_audit is already registered` → `registerAllTools` rejects → server fatal → Render rolls back silently to the 10-24 build) would have surfaced as a failed health check instead of a silent multi-day stale deploy. #2229's third falsification ("Render autoDeploy has no check-gate") is addressed on the health plane; the CI plane is option A below.
+- **Sibling status:** `browser/render.yaml` (`supremeai-browser`) **already declares** `healthCheckPath: /health` — the in-repo web-service fleet is now fully gated. The api service (`supremeai-api-ulw0`) is dashboard-managed (no in-repo blueprint); its healthCheckPath fix was routed by the RCA and tracked in #2205's post-redeploy resolution — out of repo scope, noted here only for the fleet picture. `render-worker` is a background worker: Render docs scope health checks to **web services**, so worker coverage is honestly out of B's reach (the scout's own partial-scope note).
+
+## What remains (option A — maintainer lane, ordered pair, protected path)
+
+1. **A(i) first — CI boot-smoke job per deployable service** (`.github/**` = protected path #1643, maintainer-only): build image, boot container, probe a known-good endpoint, so CI gains runtime discrimination. The RCA's causality chain is the proof this must come first: "CI stays green because Render deploys post-merge, outside GH Actions" — gating on today's CI passes broken-runtime commits (green-on-broken), a no-op gate.
+2. **A(ii) then — flip Auto-Deploy to "After CI Checks Pass"** (Render dashboard: render-primary / render-worker / render-api / mcp-tower). Official docs (render.com/docs/deploys, © 2026, fetched 2026-10-29): Render "waits for a new commit's CI checks to complete before triggering a deploy … proceeds with the deploy only if *all* checks pass"; checks count as passed on conclusion `success`, `neutral`, or `skipped`; supports GitHub Actions and checks-API integrations. Zero in-repo mentions today (`github_code_search` "After CI Checks" = 0 hits at filing).
+
+**Not recommended as first move (option C, rejected by the scout):** Deploy Hooks + autoDeploy-off pipeline triggering — new moving parts (hook secrets, pipeline coupling) before the simpler A/B pair is tried. **Option D (keep as backstop, do not duplicate):** the RCA's post-merge deploy-probe guard (`deploys[0].status != live` within N minutes → ops issue) — detection-after, complementary to A's prevention-before; the RCA already proposes it (fix #5).
+
+## Residual honesty notes
+
+- Dashboard-managed deploys: both in-repo blueprints set no `autoDeploy` key — deploy behavior lives in the Render dashboard, outside version control. Whether Render blueprints expose a CI-wait key is unverified (scout's flag); A(ii) is therefore a dashboard operation, and blueprint-izing it is a maintainer ops decision (scout alt-d, deferred not rejected).
+- The `/health` probe receipt is point-in-time; if the tower's route table changes, the gate follows the field, not this document. Blueprint field takes effect on Render's next blueprint sync / service re-create — verifying the dashboard actually picked up the field requires Render dashboard access (maintainer lane).
